{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.BreitWheelerPairProduction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.BreitWheelerPairProduction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.breit_wheeler_pair_production","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.breit_wheeler_pair_production","kind":"theorem","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/breit-wheeler-pair-production.lean#L28-L44","doc":"**Breit–Wheeler pair production** — color-threshold non-negativity\nand symmetry.\n\nTwo colored photons fuse, γγ → e⁻e⁺.  The genuine computable\ncontent of the categorical statement is that the fusion threshold\n(a) is supplied non-negatively by the two photons' Hopf-link color\ncontent, and (b) is symmetric under exchange of the two incoming\nphotons (the channel is bosonic in the photon labels).  Both are\n*derived* here — (a) from `colorWeight_pos` via `add_nonneg`, (b)\nfrom commutativity of `+` — replacing the former `True` placeholder. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.pairThreshold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.pairThreshold","kind":"def","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/breit-wheeler-pair-production.lean#L21-L26","doc":"The combined color content of two fusing photons: the threshold\nenergy supplied to the pair-production channel is carried by the\nsum (and, in the Hopf-link content, product) of the two color\nweights. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ColoredPhoton.colorWeight_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ColoredPhoton.colorWeight_pos","kind":"theorem","line":19,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/breit-wheeler-pair-production.lean#L19-L19","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ColoredPhoton.colorWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ColoredPhoton.colorWeight","kind":"def","line":18,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/breit-wheeler-pair-production.lean#L18-L18","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ColoredPhoton.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ColoredPhoton.mk","kind":"ctor","line":17,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/breit-wheeler-pair-production.lean#L17-L17","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ColoredPhoton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ColoredPhoton","kind":"structure","line":14,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/breit-wheeler-pair-production.lean#L14-L19","doc":"A colored photon is the identity element plus color dressing\nin the Hecke algebra: γ_φ = 𝟙 + φ·σ₀ + φ·σ₁. ","signatureChunk":0}]}